### 5. EmailJS Lead Submission Issue (In Progress 🔄)
- **Issue:** Lead submissions opening new email tab instead of using EmailJS
- **Root Cause:** EmailJS returning 400 error, falling back to mailto
- **Attempted Fixes:**
  - Updated template ID to match working Contact component (`template_0wxfg2m`)
  - Simplified template parameters to basic structure
  - Added better error logging and debugging
  - User manually updated template ID
- **Current Status:** Still investigating 400 error from EmailJS service
- **Next Steps:** May need to verify EmailJS template configuration or create new template

### 6. Chatbot Auto-Scroll Issue (Completed ✅)
- **Issue:** Clicking suggested prompts in ContactCoPilot forced users to scroll to bottom, requiring manual scroll back up
- **Root Cause:** useEffect auto-scroll triggered on every new message regardless of user's scroll position
- **Solution:** Implemented smart auto-scroll behavior:
  - Added messagesContainerRef to track scroll position
  - Only auto-scroll when user is within 100px of the bottom
  - Preserves user's reading position when they're viewing earlier messages
  - Maintains smooth scrolling for natural conversation flow
- **Technical Implementation:**
  - Added ref to messages container div
  - Enhanced useEffect to check scroll position before auto-scrolling
  - Uses scrollTop, scrollHeight, and clientHeight to determine if user is near bottom

### 7. White-on-White Hover Text Issue (Completed ✅)
- **Issue:** When hovering over Co-Pilot buttons, text became white on white background making it unreadable
- **Root Cause:** Hover states using very light backgrounds (hover:bg-purple-50, hover:bg-blue-50) without adjusting text color for proper contrast
- **Solution:** Enhanced hover states in ProgressiveDisclosure component:
  - Changed hover backgrounds from -50 to -100 variants for better contrast (hover:bg-purple-100, hover:bg-blue-100)
  - Added proper dark mode hover states (dark:hover:bg-purple-800/50, dark:hover:bg-blue-800/50)
  - Added hover text color changes for better contrast (hover:text-purple-800, hover:text-blue-800)
  - Added dark mode hover text colors (dark:hover:text-purple-200, dark:hover:text-blue-200)
